<newsitem itemid="109846" id="root" date="1996-10-10" xml:lang="en">
<title>NORWAY: Aker 8-month profits fall.</title>
<headline>Aker 8-month profits fall.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eight months to August 31:</p>
<p>				  (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating income	   5,547     vs	 5,367</p>
<p> Operating result		28     vs	   234</p>
<p> Result before tax	    216     vs	   538</p>
<p> EPS (crowns)		  3.48     vs	   8.19</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of offshore, cement and building materials group is AKER ASA.  </p>
<p> Ordinary writeoffs	   179     vs	   214</p>
<p> Net financial costs	    4     vs	    -6</p>
<p> Associated companies	 184     vs	   179</p>
<p> Special financial items	0     vs	    131</p>
<p> Tax				 41     vs	    135</p>
<p> After-tax result		169    vs	    398</p>
<p>NOTE - Seven analysts polled by Reuters had expected an eight-month profit before tax of 309 million crowns. Aker said the drop in profits was mainly due to a marked downturn in Norwegian Contractor's profits after a particularly good year in 1995. Aker said the 1995 figures were pro forma because of changes in the company structure.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
